[gd_scene load_steps=11 format=3]

[ext_resource type="Shader" uid="uid://rti363f5hrmg" path="res://scenes/game_object/tower/ancient_tower/ancient_tower_lvl5/ancient_tower_lvl5.gdshader" id="1"]

; The lvl5 tower's waterfalls, split out of ancient_tower_lvl5.tscn so the garage
; preview can show them too. The preview must never instance the gameplay tower —
; tower.gd._ready() calls GameState.start_run() — so the decoration lives here and
; both sides instance THIS.
;
; Found by convention: tower_preview_3d.gd looks for
;   scenes/game_object/tower/<id>/<id>_lvl<star>/<id>_lvl<star>_fx.tscn
; and adds it under the model if the file exists. A star level with no _fx scene
; simply gets nothing — no per-tower configuration anywhere.
;
; Transforms are in the .glb's local space, exactly as they were when these were
; direct children of the model instance. Do not add a transform to the root.
;
; Optimised vs. the original inline copy:
;   - 6 PlaneMesh sub-resources collapsed to 4 (three planes shared 0.07x0.47,
;     two shared 0.04x0.47) and 7 materials to 6 (two were the same colour), so
;     identical quads can batch instead of each carrying its own resource
;   - cast_shadow = 0 on every plane. They are `unshaded` + `blend_mix`, so a
;     shadow pass over them is pure cost for something that should not cast one.

